  "scene": {
    "id": "distribute-pilot3",
    "language": "So, um, our next situation is going to be, um, receiving the ball in midfield, having lots of options around you, and sort of the thought process that goes into making a decision like that, um, and knowing when to, uh, play the ball and where to play it to exactly. So, um, I think in this situation, um, I've received the ball maybe on the halfway line. My center mid- my opposing center mid has come out to pressure me. I've got, um, wingers on either side of me and strikers up front. And while it may be, you know, um, tempting to go straight to the striker, the defender's probably too close to me to make a pass like that without it being intercepted. So, my best course of action is maybe to turn to the left and try, um, to make a pass to my, you know, left or right winger and open up and receive space, uh, receive the ball in more space than I have right now, just sort of take the team forward. So, I'm going to maybe start the simulation to, um, walk you through how that looks in reality. [0]So I'm going to unpause, [1]give the ball to my player there, and make a run into[2] space. Um, at that point, now suddenly, I'm in the half space between the wingers and the attackers. I can sort of receive the ball on my back foot, turn and face to go, and I have a lot more options from that point onwards. Um...",
